  "raw_label": "-1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Durgesh Kumar Agarwal vs The State Of Jharkhand on 9 May, 2023 Author: Sanjay Kumar Dwivedi Bench: Sanjay Kumar Dwivedi In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi Cr.M.P. No. 2890 of 2013 Durgesh Kumar Agarwal ..... ... Petitioner Versus 1. The State of Jharkhand. 2. K.P. Singh, Food Inspector, Jamshedpur Camp, Seraikella-Kharsawan. ..... ... Opposite Parties -------- Coram : Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Sanjay Kumar Dwivedi ------ For the Petitioner : Mr. Navneet Sahay, Advocate.",
    "facts": "2. This petition has been filed for quashing of the entire criminal proceeding including the order taking cognizance dated 16.01.2012, by which cognizance for the offence under Section 16(i)a(i)(ii) of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 has been taken against the petitioner, in connection with G.O. No. 124 of 2011, pending in the court of learned Judicial Magistrate, Seraikella.",
    "arguments": "3. Learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that the said Act of 1954 was repealed in light of Section 97 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, in spite of that the learned court has taken the cognizance without applying its judicial mind. 4. Learned A.P.P. appearing for the State submits that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 came into effect with effect from 05.08.2011 and has replaced the earlier Act, i.e. Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 vide Government of India notification dated 04.08.2011 and the sample from the shop has been collected on 10.05.2011. He further submits that there is no illegality in the cognizance order.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "3. Learned counsel appearing for the petitioner submits that the said Act of 1954 was repealed in light of Section 97 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, in spite of that the learned court has taken the cognizance without applying its judicial mind. 4. Learned A.P.P. appearing for the State submits that Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 came into effect with effect from 05.08.2011 and has replaced the earlier Act, i.e. Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954 vide Government of India notification dated 04.08.2011 and the sample from the shop has been collected on 10.05.2011. He further submits that there is no illegality in the cognizance order.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
